# Holy Nikkah — Project Rules

> **PRIORITY:** These rules have the highest priority for this repository and must be followed in every response unless the user explicitly overrides them.

## 1. Project Overview
- Flutter app (Dart SDK `^3.8.1`), package name `holynikkah`. Matrimony/community app with VIP + Normal user tiers.
- State management: **Provider (`ChangeNotifier`)**. No Bloc/Riverpod/GetX.
- Networking: **Dio** via a single `ApiClient` wrapper returning `ApiResponse<T>`.
- Auth/backend: Firebase (`firebase_core`, `firebase_auth`) for app-level auth bootstrap + a custom REST backend.
- Architecture: **feature-first modules** under `lib/modules/<feature>/` + shared `lib/core/`.
- Navigation: **manual named routes** via `MaterialApp.routes` + `Routes` constants. NOT auto_route.
- `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` is OUTDATED (mentions auto_route/router). Trust the code, not that doc.

## 2. Context Reduction Rules (CRITICAL — follow strictly)
- NEVER scan the whole repo. Read only files directly relevant to the task.
- Use the module map below to jump straight to the right file instead of searching.
- For a feature change, read only that feature's `lib/modules/<feature>/` files + any shared core file it imports.
- Ask the user for the specific file/log/error instead of broad exploration when unsure.
- Prefer minimal diffs. Do not rewrite files or reformat unrelated code.
- Reuse existing widgets/services/utils/models before creating anything new.
- Do not read generated/build dirs: `build/`, `.dart_tool/`, `ios/`, `android/`, `assets/`.

## 3. Directory Map (use to locate code fast)
```
lib/
  main.dart                 # entry: Firebase init, FirebaseAuthService.ensureSignedIn, ApiClient.init
  application.dart          # MaterialApp, ScreenUtilInit, named routes table
  multi_provider.dart       # MultiProviderSetup — register all global providers here
  core/
    api/                    # ApiClient, ApiResponse, ApiException, interceptors/ (auth, logging, curl)
    provider/               # ThemeProvider
    services/               # session storage, firebase_auth_service, navigation_*, theme/
